		{
			icon: "mctcg:booster_pack"
			x: 3.0d
			y: -5.0d
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "Are you the champion?"
			description: [
				"&5The Feathers of Parliamant patented a unique form of digitization: in other words, converting physical matter into a digital version."
				""
				"&5Truth be told, we were working on the same technology. Except we didn't go as far as The FOP did, and we've had trouble fighting their patent in court."
				""
				"&5Both our Digitization versions converted the physical to digital.... except the soul. We stored the Soul in a magical buffer to return it when we un-digitized something. The FOP, however, digitize the soul too, which is much more dangerous for the soul..."
				""
				"&5The FOP use the Digitization tech to store EVERYTHING, and convert it later to sell. Yes, including souls."
			]
			dependencies: ["5136BFD11A07D7D0"]
			hide: true
			size: 0.75d
			id: "14923F2A5F335C80"
			tasks: [{
				id: "1A2ED7C926F72DA5"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "[Information - Digitization]"
			}]
		}
		{
			icon: {
				id: "mctcg:deckbox_white"
				Count: 1b
				tag: { }
			}
			x: 4.5d
			y: -5.0d
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "Game On!"
			description: [
				"&5The FOP Game World is a server that holds all their digitized worlds."
				""
				"&5Some of the worlds they keep as is, using them as personal kingdoms."
				""
				"&5The other worlds become part of their game. A game that includes both visiting 'Users' who think its just a fun game, and the trapped prisoners(that they call Power Users) of those worlds."
				""
				"&5These get transformed into dungeons. Everything worth money is temporarily transmuted into game items, encouraging Users and Power Users to gather them and sell them to the FOP, who return them to normal and sell them across the galaxy."
				""
				"&5Once a world is nothing but dirt and rock and other things they deem unworthy, they grind the entire world down to save server resources, and sell the remaining souls as well."
			]
			dependencies: ["1C67908469019A64"]
			hide: true
			size: 0.75d
			id: "1DC68497D620EBFE"
			tasks: [{
				id: "62EF6DA417394A01"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "[Information - FOP Game World]"
			}]
		}
		{
			x: 2.5d
			y: -1.0d
			shape: "hexagon"
			subtitle: "What's the deal?!"
			description: [
				"&5Okay, I've kind of talked your ear off here, Bandit. I need to start looking into things on my end, so I'm going to start connecting you to the other researchers here at The Ferret Business again."
				""
				"&5I'll also connect you to my sister and other co-owner of the Business, Kowa, and our second in command ByteSize. The three of us will guide you through the main issues you face."
				""
				"&5As for the other researchers, like Biologist Bitsy? They'll guide you through the finer details of the equipment, systems, and other things you'll encounter in the FOPGame Server."
				""
				"&5While I get a few things rolling, go check out The FOP Shop. I've connected it to the Q.U.E.S.T. Tablet so you can access both us and them easily."
			]
			dependencies: ["25604555CD6C8A65"]
			hide: true
			id: "31711C6DAB9BA2E5"
			tasks: [{
				id: "725D4274BB2374A0"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "Get Your Bearings"
			}]
		}
		{
			x: 2.5d
			y: 0.5d
			shape: "hexagon"
			subtitle: "Twins?"
			description: [
				"&dBack outside of the FOPServer Shop, thank the code. Right, introductions!"
				""
				"&dMy name is Kowa. As my brother, Caigan, may have mentioned, I'm his sister. Twin sister, to be precise. "
				""
				"&dWe lead The Ferret Business as a three person team, including our Vice President ByteSize, who you'll meet later.  "
				""
				"&dWe each run different parts of the Business, and it's definitely going to take all of our researchers to get you out of there. And to make the FOP pay for imprisoning you."
				""
				"&dIt's one thing to be trapped in a dimension from a teleporter accident. It's a whole 'nother level to be imprisoned in another 'dimension' against your will, yeah?"
			]
			dependencies: ["1B6761988ABBBC4A"]
			hide: true
			id: "4D05D5B4C4E8BAF2"
			tasks: [{
				id: "09E273FCEE39F305"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "The Second of Three"
			}]
		}
		{
			x: 2.5d
			y: 2.0d
			shape: "hexagon"
			subtitle: "Lots to cover!"
			description: [
				"&dAlright, I know we've talked your ears off at this point. Lots of listening, not a lot of DOING, right?"
				""
				"&dSorry, but there's a lot that needs explaining. The FOP have layered their game server with so many different systems that..."
				""
				"&7Sigh, ma'am... Let's get on with it?"
				""
				"&dHm? Oh... sorry squeaks. You're right. Bandit, this is ByteSize, company Vice President. "
				""
				"&7Yo. I think it'll be better for us to go over things as they are needed. Otherwise its a LOT to take in, yeah? Sir, Ma'am, you take charge of everything inside The Vaults. I'll take charge of things in the Mainland. Sound good?"
				""
				"&5Yep. &dGood idea."
			]
			dependencies: ["4D05D5B4C4E8BAF2"]
			hide: true
			id: "69E215271F5C1810"
			tasks: [{
				id: "03F14005B84B2D6A"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "Long Winded"
			}]
		}
		{
			x: 1.5d
			y: 3.5d
			shape: "hexagon"
			subtitle: "What's the Plan?"
			description: [
				"&5Okay, Bandit, from here we're going to separate out all the different research and exploration paths just like we did last time: into different 'quest lines', so to speak. "
				""
				"&dGamefying things isn't always bad, it's kind of what we have to do through this Q.U.E.S.T. Book. Quests, missions, goals, rewards."
				""
				"&dWell, as the squeaker said, we're talking too much. Let's get to doing, brother. "
				""
				"&5Right. Bandit, we'll handle the 'main questline', which we'll call Breaking Out."
				""
				"&dByteSize will handle explaining everything outside the Vaults, as well as connect you to different Researchers. They'll cover specific product lines, magic schools, and other things."
			]
			dependencies: ["69E215271F5C1810"]
			hide: true
			id: "110C1EFD863C907C"
			tasks: [{
				id: "0346ECC7C923F666"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "Fighting the FOP"
			}]
		}
		{
			x: 3.5d
			y: 3.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "And Everything Else"
			description: [
				"&7Phew, never thought they'd stop the exposition. Anyways, hey there Bandit! Name is ByteSize, or just Byte or Maus if you'd like. If the clues didn't give it away, I'm a mouse. Well, a computer mouse, but that's a whole other story. "
				""
				"&7I'll keep things simple: the Business owners will help you tackle the Vaults and find a way out of the FOPGame Server. Meanwhile, I'm going to help you survive and thrive in the Mainland. You'll definitely need to master both Zones to get out."
				""
				"&7The owners have a big section clearly marked Main Questline they'll handle. And other than this intro and the FOP SHOP, I'll sort out the other sections, okay? They'll cover everything else about the FOP Game Server."
				""
				"&7 Let's get started!"
			]
			dependencies: [
				"69E215271F5C1810"
				"110C1EFD863C907C"
			]
			hide: true
			id: "568F1A900320CD3F"
			tasks: [{
				id: "59F8030F2E6921DC"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "Fighting to Survive"
			}]
		}
		{
			x: 2.5d
			y: 3.0d
			shape: "pentagon"
			subtitle: "REWARDS!"
			description: [
				"&5Wait, we're forgetting something."
				""
				"&dHm? Oh, right!"
				""
				"&7Like the bosses did before, every quest, mission, etc you complete will get you a reward!"
				""
				"&5The rewards will be slightly different this time, Bandit. You'll still get money, which is a bit different this time. And you'll also get our newest Blind Bag, so new we haven't released it to market yet!"
				""
				"&7I'll cover both of those later, yeah?"
				""
				"&dOkay okay squeaker. We'll leave it at that. But first, for listening to this whole exposition dump, you'll get some money AND one of the Blind Bags...I mean, Blind Boxes."
			]
			dependencies: ["568F1A900320CD3F"]
